<title>UK: Hoverspeed ups sailings to cope with strike demand.</title>
<headline>Hoverspeed ups sailings to cope with strike demand.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hoverspeed said today it has brought forward its peak summer schedule by eleven days to cope with strong demand for fast ferries resulting from the British Airways cabin crew strike.</p>
<p>The company, which is a division of Sea Containers Ltd, said: &quot;With effect from today Hoverspeed has increased its hovercraft departures to 12 return crossings each day between Dover and Calais.&quot; Hoverspeed also operates five return crossings a day with its new SuperSeaCat fast ferry.</p>
<p>Managing director Geoffrey Ede said: &quot;With the holiday season now in full swing, and the effect of the British Airways' strike beginning to take effect, we are looking forward to a very busy summer.&quot; -Reuters Shipping News + 44 171 542 4087. Fax 5017.</p>
